     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\nDear Maely,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thanks for your interest in CODEX. You can use the codes under “CODEX for targeted sequencing” from our GitHub page <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243883109000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tKDLt6PeWvu2LXPlxI9lr\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX</a> to adapt CODEX for targeted sequencing.\r\n Note that if you have case control experimental design, for the normalization step you need to use normalize2() with normal_index specifying the sample indices for the normal samples. If all samples are all germline, you can use the default normalize() function.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Feel free to let us know if you have any further questions.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Cheers,</div>\r\n<div>Yuchao</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On May 30, 2017, at 7:46 PM, Gauthier, Marie (Health) &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Marie.G...@sa.gov.au</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nDear Nancy,</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nThat sounds great. I will wait to hear from Yuchao then</div>\r\n<div style=\"mar