rel=\"nofollow\">n...@wharton.upenn.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b><span> </span>30 May 2017 23:35<br>\r\n<b>To:</b><span> </span>Gauthier, Marie (Health)<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b><span> </span>Jiang, Yuchao<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b><span> </span>RE: Using CODEX on small custom panel (1000 genes)</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Dear Dr. Gauthier,</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Yes, we have used an updated version of CODEX (CODEX2) successfully on data from the types of designs you describe.  We are submitting the paper on this topic. \r\n I cc’d Yuchao, who is the first author on this work, and can point you to the paper’s latest draft and online code.</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Nancy</span></div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border-style:none none none solid;border-left-color:blue;border-left-width:1.5pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 4pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border-style:solid none none;border-top-color:rgb(225,225,225);border-top-width:1pt;padding:3pt 0in 0in\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span> </span>Gauthier, Marie (Health) [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailto:Marie.G...@sa.gov.au</a>]<span> </span><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b><span> </span>Tuesday, May 30, 2017 12:11 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b><span> </span>Zhang, Nancy R &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">n...@wharton.upenn.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b><span> </span>Using CODEX on small custom panel (1000 genes)</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">\r\n </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif;background-color:white;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;background-color:white\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Dear Nancy Zhang,</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;background-color:white\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Is it possible to use CODEX for a small gene panel? The panel in question is a custom-designed Roche/Nimblegen panel of around 1000 coding genes (it enriches for exonic regions).</span></div>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;background-color:white;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;background-color:white\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Kind 